tor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOTA, YASUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An object-to-be-printed detector for judging whether an object-to-be-printed is made of plane paper or of special paper. The detector comprises an infrared sensor for detecting infrared radiation (4) radiated from an object (1) heated by heating means (2) to judge whether the object is made of plane paper or special paper.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un détecteur d'objet à imprimer est capable de juger si un objet à imprimer est en papier ordinaire ou en papier spécial. Le détecteur comprend un capteur infrarouge qui détecte le rayonnement infrarouge (4) émis par un objet (1) chauffé par un dispositif (2) chauffant afin de juger si l'objet est en papier ordinaire ou en papier spécial.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>